        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000041",
          "event_id": "ed3c4e3f-3a74-4ce9-88e9-b3d1535b0e95",
          "field": "response",
          "start": 122,
          "end": 265,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "다만 Offline-first와 서버가 없는 구조(Serverless가 아닌 Local-only)는 구분해야 해. Offline-first는 인터넷 연결 없이도 주요 기능이 작동하도록 설계하는 접근법이고, 반드시 서버를 사용하지 않는다는 의미는 아니야.\n\n",
          "selected": false
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000152",
          "event_id": "cea924fc-a959-4e71-8805-3074f62960c3",
          "field": "text",
          "start": 2570,
          "end": 2894,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "Note that, in addition to the above, browsers will store other types of data in the browser for an origin, such as\nWebAssembly\ncode caching.\nDoes browser-stored data persist?\nData for an origin can be stored in two ways in a browser,\npersistent\nand\nbest-effort\n:\nBest-effort: this is the way that data is stored by default. ",
          "selected": false
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000153",
          "event_id": "cea924fc-a959-4e71-8805-3074f62960c3",
          "field": "text",
          "start": 2894,
          "end": 3370,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "Best-effort data persists as long as the origin is below its quota, the device has enough storage space, and the user doesn't choose to delete the data via their browser's settings.\nPersistent: an origin can opt-in to store its data in a persistent way. Data stored this way is only evicted, or deleted, if the user chooses to, by using their browser's settings. To learn more, see\nWhen is data evicted\n.\nThe data stored in the browser by an origin is best-effort by default. ",
          "selected": true
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000154",
          "event_id": "cea924fc-a959-4e71-8805-3074f62960c3",
          "field": "text",
          "start": 3370,
          "end": 3840,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "When using web technologies such as IndexedDB or Cache, the data is stored transparently without asking for the user's permission. Similarly, when the browser needs to evict best-effort data, it does so without interrupting the user.\nIf, for any reason, developers need persistent storage (e.g., when building a web app that relies on critical data that isn't persisted anywhere else), they can do so by using the\nnavigator.storage.persist()\nmethod of the\nStorage API\n.\n",
          "selected": true
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000155",
          "event_id": "cea924fc-a959-4e71-8805-3074f62960c3",
          "field": "text",
          "start": 3840,
          "end": 4272,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "In Firefox, when a site chooses to use persistent storage, the user is notified with a UI popup that their permission is requested.\nSafari and most Chromium-based browsers, such as Chrome or Edge, automatically approve or deny the request based on the user's history of interaction with the site and do not show any prompts to the user.\nNote that\nresearch from the Chrome team\nshows that data is very rarely deleted by the browser. ",
          "selected": false
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "G000177",
          "event_id": "3d95ae56-0184-4ec8-9c79-edcd4bfb91ce",
          "field": "question",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 136,
          "offset_unit": "utf16_code_units",
          "quote": "MDN 문서를 보니 IndexedDB로 브라우저에 데이터를 저장할 수 있네. 그렇다면 초기 MVP에서는 별도 클라우드 데이터베이스 없이 IndexedDB만 사용하는게 합리적이라는 가설을 세울 수 있겠어. 이 판단에서 놓치고 있는 위험이 있을까?",
